    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) and **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90) leading the charge. **Vinnie Pasquantino** is our premier play, leveraging a substantial +16% park adjustment and a prime +14% platoon edge against Bradish, while **Seiya Suzuki**\u2019s score is inflated by a significant +8% historical BvP advantage and a favorable matchup against a struggling Lodolo. **Brice Turang** (73.19) remains a priority start despite the weather risk; his 100% stolen base efficiency potential against Chandler\u2019s slow delivery makes him vital to our pursuit of the scarcest category in this 5x5 format.\n\nWe are navigating a few volatile situations, most notably the rain risks hovering over **Seiya Suzuki**, **Brice Turang**, and **Edwin Arroyo**. While **James Wood** (53.19) projects lower than our core, his elite .432 xwOBA and leadoff position secure his spot, though he faces a stiff test against Schlittler. **Corbin Carroll** (59.02) remains in the lineup despite a -15% drag from Yamamoto\u2019s skill set, as his stolen base upside is simply too high to bench. The most difficult decision this morning was leaving **Josh Naylor** (53.42) on the bench. He missed the final cut by a hair\u2014falling just shy of the efficiency floor set by the high-ceiling platoon plays like **Mickey Moniak**\u2014largely due to a park penalty and the negative impact of facing Jax. Keep an eye on **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**; as their lineups are still pending, any shift in their batting order could necessitate a quick pivot to maintain our efficiency targets.",
